    <div class="acting_info container">
        <h6>
            <br> <b> Bollywood</b><br><br> is the informal term used to refer to the Hindi-language film industry based
            in Mumbai,
            India.
            It is one of the largest and most prominent film industries in the world, known for producing a vast
            number of films each year. Here's some key information about Bollywood:

            <br> <br> <b> Origin:</b> <br> The term "Bollywood" is a portmanteau of "Bombay" (the former name of Mumbai)
            and
            "Hollywood"
            (the American film industry). Bollywood's roots can be traced back to the early 20th century, and it has
            since grown into a major global film industry.

            <br> <br> <b> Language:</b> <br> Most Bollywood films are made in the Hindi language, although there are
            also
            films made in
            other Indian languages, such as Tamil, Telugu, Bengali, and more. Bollywood's global recognition
            primarily comes from its Hindi-language productions.

            <br> <br> <b> Genres:</b> <br> Bollywood produces a wide range of film genres, including romantic dramas,
            action
            films,
            comedies, musicals, thrillers, and historical epics. Music and dance are integral components of most
            Bollywood movies, with elaborate song-and-dance sequences being a hallmark.

            <br> <br> <b> Film Production:</b> <br> Bollywood is known for its prolific film production, with hundreds
            of
            movies released
            each year. The industry is supported by a vast network of studios, production houses, and professionals,
            making it a major economic driver in India.

            <br> <br> <b>Superstars:</b> <br>Bollywood has a roster of iconic actors and actresses who have achieved
            international fame.
            Some well-known Bollywood stars include Amitabh Bachchan, Shah Rukh Khan, Aishwarya Rai Bachchan,
            Priyanka Chopra, and Deepika Padukone, among many others.

            <br> <br> <b> Film Music:</b> <br> Bollywood is also famous for its music, and songs from Bollywood films
            often
            become
            chart-toppers in India and beyond. Renowned music directors and playback singers contribute to the
            industry's vibrant musical culture.

            <br> <br> <b> Global Reach:</b> <br>Bollywood movies have a substantial global audience, with a fan base in
            many
            countries.
            Indian expatriates, as well as non-Indian audiences, appreciate Bollywood films for their colorful
            storytelling, music, and dance.

            <br> <br> <b> Awards:</b><br> Bollywood has its own set of awards and honors, including the National Film
            Awards
            and the
            Filmfare Awards, which recognize excellence in various categories such as acting, direction, music, and
            more.

            <br><br> <b>Influence on Fashion and Culture:</b><br> Bollywood has a significant influence on fashion
            trends
            and cultural
            elements in India and among the Indian diaspora. Costumes worn by actors and actresses in films often
            set trends, and Bollywood's portrayal of Indian culture and traditions can shape societal norms.

            <br> <br> <b> Evolution:</b><br> Over the years, Bollywood has evolved to reflect changing societal values
            and
            global trends.
            Filmmakers have tackled a wider range of themes, including social issues, politics, and contemporary
            topics, in addition to traditional love stories and family dramas.

            <br> Bollywood continues to be a major force in the world of cinema, blending traditional Indian
            storytelling
            with modern cinematic techniques. Its global reach and cultural impact make it a significant component
            of India's entertainment and cultural landscape.
        </h6>
    </div>

